00:02:23.864 --> 00:02:28.467
Now compare that with an app that friends praise but nobody buys.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.384
The feedback may be useful.

00:02:30.384 --> 00:02:33.836
It does not yet show that customers will pay.

00:02:33.836 --> 00:02:39.973
A purchase gives stronger evidence of paying demand, although one sale does not prove long-term success.

00:02:39.973 --> 00:02:44.192
Remember the objective: identify customer, offer, delivery in a simple example.

00:02:44.512 --> 00:02:51.739
When you examine an idea, ask: who is the customer, what is the offer, and how will it be delivered?

